Vamp's own changes to BlueZ 5.88 for any base (docs/bluez.md#bases), applied by tools/thirdparty.py's
build_bluez. Licensed as the code it changes, GPL-2.0-or-later. Nothing here names libbtctl or any of
Shanling's code: their hooks are a patch of their own, applied only for the stock base.

- main.conf [GATT] Server (default true): false leaves out the GATT database, the LE advertising manager
  and the advertisement monitor manager on every adapter, through the path upstream already takes for a
  controller without LE, so nothing listens on the LE attribute channel (L2CAP CID 4) and coda-rc serves
  it and advertises through the kernel itself, as under stock's bluetoothd
  (docs/bluez.md#the-le-attribute-channel). LE scanning, pairing and the GATT client stay.

diff --git a/src/adapter.c b/src/adapter.c
index 6588a6e..bbff13c 100644
--- a/src/adapter.c
+++ b/src/adapter.c
@@ -9918,10 +9918,13 @@ static int adapter_register(struct btd_adapter *adapter)
 		btd_ranging_provider_manager_create(adapter);
 
 	/* Don't start GATT database and advertising managers on
-	 * non-LE controllers.
+	 * non-LE controllers, nor where main.conf's [GATT] Server is false:
+	 * then another program may serve the LE attribute channel and
+	 * advertise through the kernel itself.
 	 */
 	if (!(adapter->supported_settings & MGMT_SETTING_LE) ||
-					btd_opts.mode == BT_MODE_BREDR)
+					btd_opts.mode == BT_MODE_BREDR ||
+					!btd_opts.gatt_server)
 		goto load;
 
 	adapter->database = btd_gatt_database_new(adapter);
